{
  "id": "30008_uchitoru",
  "headword": "{打|う}ち{取|と}る",
  "reading": "うちとる",
  "romaji": "uchitoru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to retire a batter; to get (a batter) out",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to retire a batter; to get (a batter) out (baseball)",
      "explanation": "(of a pitcher or the fielding side) to put a batter out without allowing a hit, often by inducing a weak grounder or fly ball."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30008_uchitoru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{投手|とうしゅ}は{打者|だしゃ}を{打|う}ち{取|と}った。",
      "english": "The pitcher retired the batter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30008_uchitoru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{内野|ないや}ゴロで{打者|だしゃ}を{打|う}ち{取|と}る。",
      "english": "To retire the batter with an infield grounder.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30008_uchitoru_ex3",
      "japanese": "エースは{最後|さいご}の{打者|だしゃ}をピッチャーゴロに{打|う}ち{取|と}って{試合|しあい}を{締|し}めた。",
      "english": "The ace retired the last batter with a grounder to the mound, closing out the game.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive; takes the retired batter as the を object.\n\nA baseball term for getting a batter out. Often specifies how the out was made:\n- {内野|ないや}ゴロに{打|う}ち{取|と}る: to retire with an infield grounder\n- {凡打|ぼんだ}に{打|う}ち{取|と}る: to induce an easy out\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {討|う}ち{取|と}る: to slay; to defeat (an enemy in battle) — a homophone written with a different kanji",
